      "side": 1,
      "message": "Stream.max with this comparator that returns 0 for any date-vs-semver\npair can lead to a scenario, where a genuinely compatible model gets dropped. That comparator is not a TOTAL order, so \"max\" keeps whichever element it encountered first (among non-comparable ones). Let\u0027s say \n- module \"foo\" is stored as both \"2021-01-01\" (date) and \"2.5.0\" (semver).\n- the device requests \"2.0.0\". If iteration yields the date first, \"max\" keeps \"2021-01-01\"\n- isBackwardsCompatible(\"2021-01-01\",\"2.0.0\") is mixed-scheme, returns 0\n- the model is DROPPED, even though the compatible \"2.5.0\" was present. \nThe outcome depends on datastore iteration order.",
      "revId": "10af1e3be559acab8bafd8c5da9be5e73c348cdb",
      "serverId": "7fc14799-209e-464c-9743-7a06c2c21a81"
